    "details": "<p><strong>SIGNAL QUEST &ndash; IEEE SPS HACKATHON 2026</strong></p>\n<p>We have an important update regarding the <strong>Signal Quest &ndash; IEEE SPS Hackathon 2026</strong>, happening at <strong>CMR Institute of Technology, Bengaluru</strong> on <strong>26 September 2026</strong>.</p>\n<h3>REGISTRATION FEE WAIVED OFF</h3>\n<p>The <strong>registration fee has been completely waived off</strong> for the hackathon!</p>\n<p>If you have already paid the registration fee, <strong>the amount will be refunded to you</strong>.</p>\n<h3>️ IMPORTANT: OFFICIAL WEBSITE REGISTRATION IS COMPULSORY</h3>\n<p>Registering through <strong>Unstop alone is NOT sufficient</strong>.</p>\n<p>All participants/teams <strong>MUST register through the official Signal Quest website</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>Official Website:</strong><br /><a href=\"https://signal-quest-drab.vercel.app/\">https://signal-quest-drab.vercel.app/</a></p>\n<p>Even if you have already registered through Unstop, please make sure you complete the registration on the <strong>official website as well</strong>.</p>\n<h3>ATTENDANCE REQUIREMENT</h3>\n<p>Participants who register through the official website are expected to <strong>attend the hackathon in person</strong>.</p>\n<p>This is a <strong>10-hour offline hackathon</strong>, so please register only if you are available to attend on <strong>26 September 2026</strong>.</p>\n<h3>EVENT DETAILS</h3>\n<p><strong>Date:</strong> 26 September 2026<br /><strong>Time:</strong> 8:00 AM &ndash; 6:00 PM<br /><strong>Venue:</strong> CMR Institute of Technology, Bengaluru<br /><strong>Team Size:</strong> 1&ndash;4 members<br /><strong>Registration Fee:</strong> FREE<br /><strong>Prize Pool:</strong> ₹14,000<br /><strong>Refreshments:</strong> Refreshments will be provided to all participants.</p>\n<p><strong>Certificates to all the participants will be provided.</strong></p>\n<h3>CHALLENGE TRACKS</h3>\n<p>Participants can build their solution under any one of the following tracks:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Speech &amp; Audio AI</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Computer Vision</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Biomedical Signals</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>AI &amp; Machine Learning</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Wireless &amp; IoT</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Sustainable Technologies</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Open Innovation</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Embedded Systems</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Teams will have <strong>10 hours to develop, prototype, and present their solution</strong> to the judging panel.</p>\n<h3>⏳ REGISTRATION DEADLINE</h3>\n<p><strong>20 September 2026</strong></p>\n<p>Students from different colleges and different engineering branches/specializations can form a team. Each team can have a maximum of <strong>4 members</strong>.</p>\n<p>Please make sure to <strong>complete your registration on the official website</strong> and register only if you are able to attend the hackathon in person.</p>\n<p><strong>Think Big. Think Bold. Think 10X.</strong></p>",
